# text = And it came to pass that when Jesus had spoken these words unto Nephi, and to those who had been called, (now the number of them who had been called, and received power and authority to baptize, was twelve) and behold, he stretched forth his hand unto the multitude, and cried unto them, saying: Blessed are ye if ye shall give heed unto the words of these twelve whom I have chosen from among you to minister unto you, and to be your servants; and unto them I have given power that they may baptize you with water; and after that ye are baptized with water, behold, I will baptize you with fire and with the Holy Ghost; therefore blessed are ye if ye shall believe in me and be baptized, after that ye have seen me and know that I am.
# sent_id = 337
# llm_note = AICTP frame: it(2)=expl, came(3)=root, to pass(4-5)=xcomp, that(6)=mark on "stretched"(50, main event in ccomp advcl). Temporal when-clause (7-22): "when Jesus had spoken...unto Nephi, and to those who had been called". Parenthetical (24-45): "now the number...was twelve" = parataxis on root or on "stretched". "behold"(47) = INTJ discourse. Main event: "he stretched forth his hand...and cried...saying:". The "saying:" introduces reported speech (ccomp of "cried"). Reported speech contains three major segments separated by semicolons: (a) "Blessed are ye if ye shall give heed...servants"; (b) "unto them I have given power that they may baptize you with water"; (c) "after that ye are baptized...I will baptize you...therefore blessed are ye...". The final "Blessed are ye" is the apodosis of "if ye shall believe and be baptized". "after that ye have seen me and know that I am" = temporal advcl.
